X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/snapshots-of-the-wild-what-are-trail-cameras-teaching-us/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T120000
DTSTAMP:20261119T152742Z
CREATED:20261119T152742Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261119T152742Z
UID:1778780020273-1795255200-1795262400@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Snapshots of the Wild: What are trail cameras teaching us?
DESCRIPTION:Snapshots of the Wild! What are trail cameras teaching us\nSaturday\, November 21  |  10am – 12pm \nFREE Education Program for youth and families \nN – Core  |  BREG – Elective \nRegister Here! \nEver wondered what wildlife is doing when nobody is looking? Join ecoEXPLORE on Saturday\, November 21 for our next Mammalogy Season Skill Session where young explorers can learn all about trail cameras\, how they work\, and their role in wildlife research. After learning about trail photography and investigating mammal signs outside we’ll welcome naturalist Carlton Burke who will introduce us to a furry friend! \nWant to dive deeper down the burrow? Adults and seasoned ecoEXPLORERS can pre-register for Mammals of the Southern Appalachians\, a longer class with expert naturalist Carlton Burke from 12pm-4pm. Come investigate\, discover\, and learn more about mammals all day at The North Carolina Arboretum!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/snapshots-of-the-wild-what-are-trail-cameras-teaching-us/
CATEGORIES:EcoExplore
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Random-Program-Graphics-64.png
END:VEVENT
