X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ashevillehikinggroup
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_317499143@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064704Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T133000
SUMMARY:Bent Creek Wolf Knob Loop - 8.5 Miles\, 1600 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nBack to Bent Creek. This loop star
 ts at Rice Pinnacle parking lot\, goes up to Wolf Knob and then loops arou
 nd and back down Boyd Branch. This loop has some easier fire road trails a
 long with one steep climb up and down. Some of these trails are mountain b
 ike trails although we don't tend to see many on a Monday morning.\n\nThis
  is a hard hike. Expect rocky\, rooty trail\, steep climbs\, and steep up 
 and downhills. In fall\, leaves can hide rocks and roots and make footing 
 slippery. We will keep a moderate pace when possible (last time we had a m
 oving avg of 2.8 mph). Please only sign up if you're comfortable with stee
 p\, uneven terrain and hiking 8.5 miles. If you're not sure\, message me f
 irst and I'm happy to talk it through.\n\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/explor
 e/custom-routes/rice-pinnacle-parking-to-wolf-knob-to-boyd-branch-2f0b4c5\
 n\n**CARPOOL**\nI don't think a carpool is necessary for this one but feel
  free to arrange something via event chat or comments.\n\n**WEATHER**\nThe
  weather currently might be okay for Monday but I'll watch the weather and
  post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM if there is a chance of severe wea
 ther or lightning during this time period..\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can mes
 sage me through MeetUp or phone until the hike starts although cell recept
 ion may be sketchy\, (508) 965-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hikin
 g Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from 
 the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety and aff
 irm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipm
 ent\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neit
 her your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety 
 nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full responsibility for any i
 njuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/317499143
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261119T152109Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261119T152109Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Mountains To Sea Trail Hiking Club": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiking-club/events/317341246/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_mountains_to_sea_trail_hiking_club
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_317341246@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064705Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T110000
SUMMARY:Mountains-to-Sea Trail Highway 25 toward Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a fa
 irly easy hike\, and we go at a high average to low advanced speed\, which
  is roughly about 3.0 to 3.2 mph. There are no super long hills. It's pret
 ty undulating all the way.\n\nWell behaved dogs on leashes are welcome to 
 attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park at the gravel lot across from the trail 
 head. You'll see some people gathering by their cars. I've recently correc
 ted the PIN setting on the map\, so it should be correct. Here are some di
 rections to use too: When going south on Hendersonville Road\, go past Car
 olina Day School and turn right at the Blue Ridge Parkway exit. When you g
 et to the parkway turn RIGHT. You will see parking on the left and right s
 ide of the road. Park there.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are designed 
 for fitness and community among people who are already reasonably fit. It'
 s not an endurance hike by any means\, but it is designed so we can get ou
 r hearts beating a bit while still being able to have a conversation and m
 eet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce ourselves
  briefly. There will be a person who is a sweep. This person is the person
  who walks last and makes sure no one gets lost.\n\nWe leave the parking s
 pot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature break\, we wait fo you\, but it's n
 ot a hike where we stop and take photos or frequent breaks. We basically k
 eep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, then turn around after a short (approx
 imately 5 minute) break. Then we keep that same pace on the way back. If w
 e get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are normally finished around 10:50.\n\
 nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning that we hike in and turn around ha
 lf way to return back.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/317341246/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261108T161702Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261108T161702Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
