X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Avl Digital Nomads": "https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/315657080/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_avl_digital_nomads
X-SOURCE:AVL Digital Nomads
UID:event_315657080@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064708Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T193000
SUMMARY:AVL Digital Nomads - Book Club
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n**December 2026 Selection - *When Breach B
 ecomes Air* by Paul Kalanithi**\n[Amazon](https://www.amazon.com/When-Brea
 th-Becomes-Paul-Kalanithi/dp/081298840X/) - [GoodReads](https://www.goodre
 ads.com/book/show/25899336-when-breath-becomes-)\n\n*At the age of thirty-
 six\, on the verge of completing a decade’s worth of training as a neuro
 surgeon\, Paul Kalanithi was diagnosed with stage IV lung cancer. One day 
 he was a doctor treating the dying\, and the next he was a patient struggl
 ing to live. And just like that\, the future he and his wife had imagined 
 evaporated. When Breath Becomes Air chronicles Kalanithi’s transformatio
 n from a naïve medical student “possessed\,” as he wrote\, “by the 
 question of what\, given that all organisms die\, makes a virtuous and mea
 ningful life” into a neurosurgeon at Stanford working in the brain\, the
  most critical place for human identity\, and finally into a patient and n
 ew father confronting his own mortality.*\n\n*What makes life worth living
  in the face of death? What do you do when the future\, no longer a ladder
  toward your goals in life\, flattens out into a perpetual present? What d
 oes it mean to have a child\, to nurture a new life as another fades away?
  These are some of the questions Kalanithi wrestles with in this profoundl
 y moving\, exquisitely observed memoir.*\n\n*Paul Kalanithi died in March 
 2015\, while working on this book\, yet his words live on as a guide and a
  gift to us all. “I began to realize that coming face to face with my ow
 n mortality\, in a sense\, had changed nothing and everything\,” he wrot
 e. “Seven words from Samuel Beckett began to repeat in my head: ‘I can
 ’t go on. I’ll go on.’” When Breath Becomes Air is an unforgettabl
 e\, life-affirming reflection on the challenge of facing death and on the 
 relationship between doctor and patient\, from a brilliant writer who beca
 me both.*\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n**Welcome to our monthly Book Club!** We’re
  a small\, friendly group that gets together for fun\, thoughtful conversa
 tions about a different book each month.\n\nFinished the whole book? Great
 . Only made it through a few chapters? Still come. Didn’t read it at all
  but the discussion sounds interesting? Honestly\, you’re welcome too.\n
 We meet on the **first Tuesday of every month**.\n\nOne of the best things
  about this group is that we keep it relatively small and guide the conver
 sation\, so it doesn’t turn into three people talking while everyone els
 e quietly questions their life choices. Everyone has a chance to jump in\,
  share their thoughts\, and explore the book’s characters\, themes\, wri
 ting\, and bigger ideas.\n\nYou definitely don’t need to be a literary e
 xpert. Whether you read constantly or you’re trying to get back into it\
 , this is a relaxed place to discover new books\, hear different perspecti
 ves\, and meet some great people along the way.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/315657080/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260712T190922Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260712T190922Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Avl Digital Nomads": "https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/317179110/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_avl_digital_nomads
X-SOURCE:AVL Digital Nomads
UID:event_317179110@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064708Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T200000
SUMMARY:The Next Five: Build ADN’s 2027 Together
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nEver wondered how AVL Digital Nomads actua
 lly works\, who makes it happen\, and where it’s headed next? Come find 
 out\, and help decide.\n\nADN has almost 6\,000 members and zero employees
 . Every social\, lunch\, book club\, and workshop on our calendar exists b
 ecause a nomad decided it should. This evening is a look behind the curtai
 n: where we’ve been\, where we’re going\, and the many ways to be part
  of it. It’s built as much for people who joined this year as for longti
 me regulars.\n\nWe’re gathering where ADN began in 2021: Wedge Brewing a
 t Foundation\, in the new community room they built after Helene. It felt 
 like the right place to start the next chapter.\n\n**What happens**\n\n* *
 *Where ADN is headed:** A short\, honest look at the mission and what’s 
 next.\n* **“My First Event” stories:** Longtime organizers share how t
 hey got started\, mishaps included.\n* **The Idea Wall:** Ideas from RSVPs
  go up on the wall. Add yours and vote with dot stickers. Have an idea alr
 eady? Share it when you RSVP. It’s optional\n* **The No-Shark Tank:** An
 yone can pitch an event idea in 60 seconds. Nobody gets eaten\, and listen
 ing counts.\n* **Huddles:** Join the conversation that interests you. Some
  people leave with a plan\, and everyone leaves knowing more nomads than t
 hey came with.\n\nCome curious. No idea\, commitment\, or experience requi
 red.\n\nPlenty of free parking.\nNon-alcoholic drinks available.\nFood tru
 ck: Burger Boy
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/317179110/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261028T183436Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261028T183436Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Shutupandwriteasheville": "https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/317388315/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_shutupandwriteasheville
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_317388315@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064732Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261201T193000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write!® - Downtown
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\n***\\*\\*\\*Please 
 note: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this M
 eetup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\n**Here's how it works
 .** Show up at or before 6:00. At 6:00\, we do some quick introductions. A
 fterward\, for a full 60 minutes (I'll set a timer!) we are heads-down wri
 ting. Writing what? A novel? You bet. Some poetry? Sure. Song lyrics? Your
  resume? That report you need to get to your boss before 8 AM or you'll *n
 eed* *to write* that resume? All of the above and more. Just shut up and w
 rite.\n\nSurrounding ourselves with other writers who are busy putting wor
 ds onto page (physical or virtual) keeps us all accountable and focused.\n
 \nWhen the timer goes off\, we'll check-in with each other and see how it 
 went. Afterward\, feel free to stay to chat and get to know your fellow wr
 iters\, or keep writing\, or take off.\n\nSocializing is optional and will
  happen after (or briefly before) the focused writing. This is a safe spac
 e to work on your craft. No one will read or critique your writing.\n\nFor
  more information about our events\, visit [https://shutupwrite.com](https
 ://shutupwrite.com).\n\n**What to Expect**\n\n* Roughly 15 minutes of intr
 oductions\n* 60 minutes of focused writing (somebody set a timer)!\n* Afte
 rward\, optional socializing\n\n**Being late is okay:** Just show up and g
 et settled\, then check in with the host after the session. (Look for the 
 person with the Shut Up & Write sign).\n\n**What Should I Bring?**\n\n* Wh
 atever you need to be able to write!\n* Earbuds/earplugs if you want to bl
 ock ambient noise.\n\n**Other Important Details:**\n\n***\\*\\*\\*Please n
 ote: Shut Up & Write event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! web
 site and this Meetup page will be closed. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\nHOSTS: This is a mult
 i-host event\, so most of the time there will be a host present. If we are
  unlucky and no host can attend\, please find each other and self-organize
 . Pay attention to the event chat and comments to see who is available.\n\
 nWI-FI: Yes!\n\nPARKING: Street parking in metered spots is free after 6pm
 . Closest municipal garages ($2/hour) are Wall St. & Coxe Street/Sears All
 ey.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/317388
 315/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261111T230745Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T230745Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
