SUMMARY:Gaming Night @ Noble Cider
DESCRIPTION:Asheville's Bored Game Geeks\nRoll the dice and pour a glass! 
 🎲🍎\n\nGaming Night is back at Noble Cider! Join us every other Tuesd
 ay for a night of tabletop tactics\, card-shuffling chaos\, and great comp
 any. Whether you’re a seasoned strategist or you still think a "meeple" 
 is a type of small fruit\, you’re welcome at our table.\n\n### The Lowdo
 wn:\n\n* **No Experience? No Problem:** We’re all about community. We’
 ll help you learn the ropes of a new game or cheer you on while you figure
  it out.\n* **The Library:** We have a solid stash of games ready to play
 —from quick party favorites to deeper strategy titles.\n* **Bring Your F
 avorites:** Have a game gathering dust on your shelf? Bring it along! We l
 ove seeing what the community is playing.\n* **The Vibe:** High-quality ci
 der\, cozy atmosphere\, and just the right amount of competitive spirit.\n
 \n**Feel Free to bring your own games too!**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevilles-bored-game-geeks/events/31
 7434935/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261115T011739Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261115T011739Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Avl Digital Nomads": "https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/317383186/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_avl_digital_nomads
X-SOURCE:AVL Digital Nomads
UID:event_317383186@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064708Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T200000
SUMMARY:Why Your Resolutions Fail by February (and How to Make This Year D
 ifferent)
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nEvery January we set big intentions\, and 
 by February most of them have quietly disappeared. It’s rarely about wil
 lpower. Usually two things get in the way: practical obstacles we haven’
 t planned for\, and beliefs running underneath that pull us back to the ol
 d pattern.\n\nIn this 2-hour evening workshop\, you’ll design the year y
 ou want and then take apart what’s been stopping you\, at both levels.\n
 \n**What we’ll do together:**\n\n* Take a guided meditation into your id
 eal life\, to get clear on what you really want.\n* Map your goals across 
 the six key areas of life\n* Pick one goal and identify its practical obst
 acles\, then turn them into simple\, doable next steps\n* Uncover any beli
 efs holding you back from your goal and keeping you stuck.\n* Learn neurop
 lasticity-based tools you can use on your own to start rewiring that belie
 f keeping you stuck.\n\nYou’ll leave with a clear goal\, a realistic set
  of the first few baby steps and a worksheet to keep using all year.\n\n**
 Who it’s for:** remote workers\, freelancers\, founders and anyone tired
  of starting the year strong and fading by spring.\n**What to bring:** the
  goal you’re tired of failing at. Worksheets provided.\n**Your host:** J
 amie Leavitt is a certified coach\, an RTT® hypnotherapist and the founde
 r of The Inner Rewrite. After 25 years in corporate including 13 coaching 
 leaders\, she now helps high achievers get to the root of what keeps them 
 stuck.\nSpots are limited to 40.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-digital-nomads/events/317383186/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261111T163143Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T163143Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Shutupandwriteasheville": "https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/317488766/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_shutupandwriteasheville
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_317488766@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T064732Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T193000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write!® - Downtown
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\n***\\*\\*\\*Please 
 note: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this M
 eetup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\n**Here's how it works
 .** Show up at or before 6:00. At 6:00\, we do some quick introductions. A
 fterward\, for a full 60 minutes (I'll set a timer!) we are heads-down wri
 ting. Writing what? A novel? You bet. Some poetry? Sure. Song lyrics? Your
  resume? That report you need to get to your boss before 8 AM or you'll *n
 eed* *to write* that resume? All of the above and more. Just shut up and w
 rite.\n\nSurrounding ourselves with other writers who are busy putting wor
 ds onto page (physical or virtual) keeps us all accountable and focused.\n
 \nWhen the timer goes off\, we'll check-in with each other and see how it 
 went. Afterward\, feel free to stay to chat and get to know your fellow wr
 iters\, or keep writing\, or take off.\n\nSocializing is optional and will
  happen after (or briefly before) the focused writing. This is a safe spac
 e to work on your craft. No one will read or critique your writing.\n\nFor
  more information about our events\, visit [https://shutupwrite.com](https
 ://shutupwrite.com).\n\n**What to Expect**\n\n* Roughly 15 minutes of intr
 oductions\n* 60 minutes of focused writing (somebody set a timer)!\n* Afte
 rward\, optional socializing\n\n**Being late is okay:** Just show up and g
 et settled\, then check in with the host after the session. (Look for the 
 person with the Shut Up & Write sign).\n\n**What Should I Bring?**\n\n* Wh
 atever you need to be able to write!\n* Earbuds/earplugs if you want to bl
 ock ambient noise.\n\n**Other Important Details:**\n\n***\\*\\*\\*Please n
 ote: Shut Up & Write event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! web
 site and this Meetup page will be closed. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\nHOSTS: This is a mult
 i-host event\, so most of the time there will be a host present. If we are
  unlucky and no host can attend\, please find each other and self-organize
 . Pay attention to the event chat and comments to see who is available.\n\
 nWI-FI: Yes!\n\nPARKING: Street parking in metered spots is free after 6pm
 . Closest municipal garages ($2/hour) are Wall St. & Coxe Street/Sears All
 ey.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/317488
 766/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261118T230404Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T230404Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
